@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.provisioning.lcs.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To LCS Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account integration to LCS works properly.

Setup:
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | lcs.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | LCS                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |

Teardown:
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production         |
	| DXP Non-Production     |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Management Tools (LCS) |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korlcs - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onelcs - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORLCSKORLCS |
	| ONELCSONELCS |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KORLCSKORLCS |
	| ONELCSONELCS |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korlcs - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onelcs - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View project
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to integrate a project from provisioning to LCS

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLCSKORLCS                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I generate the product purchase ID value for the product purchase made by "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Management Tools (LCS)" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 0 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 0 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| LCS User        |
	| Support Watcher |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korlcs"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the Sync To LCS button on the account page
	And I wait for "6" minutes
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I log into the lcs homepage as "patricia.draut@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the lcs support page
	And I search the lcs support index using the corp project id "${staticAccountId}"
	Then I should be able to view a project on the lcs support index with the name "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name                  | Korlcs - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Corp Project ID       | ${staticAccountId}            |
	| Subscription Type     | PRODUCTION                    |
	| Servers Used          | 0                             |
	| Servers Allowed       | 1                             |
	| Subscription End Date | ${staticFullEndDate}          |
	| Support End Date      | ${staticFullEndDate}          |

Scenario: View project with consumption
	Testing the ability to integrate a project with a consumption from provisioning to LCS

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORLCSKORLCS                         |
	| Contact Email Address | lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | lcs.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Active                               |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I generate the account key value for "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate static full start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korlcs - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
